        "cooked": "<p>Well, I have formally welcomed all four new villains into the fold by beating them up with their nemeses. &nbsp;Then Ennead in particular folded impressively - I was pressed for time so I went after them with Argent Adept, Ra, Legacy, Nightmist, and Haka. &nbsp;I opened with Syncopated Onslaught, Staff of Ra, Inspiring Presence, Oblivion, and Rampage, and followed that up with a Drawn to the Flame and Imbued Fire on the next few turns. &nbsp;I think that the Ennead did less damage to the heroes than the heroes themselves. &nbsp;And Drawn to the Flame was dealing 6 damage per villain purely on the basis of damage boosts (+2 from Legacy, +1 from AA, +2 from Staff and Imbued Fire, +1 for Nemesis)</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:21:30.849Z",
