      {
        "id": 143999,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-07-07T14:35:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>One thing I've noticed is that Argent Adept has single-handedly doubled how long my games take as I try to figure out how to use every one of his instruments and songs each turn. He's also keeping everyone healed and buffed and made sure the environment and ongoing cards didn't do jack (took on Voss, destroyed Forced Deployment, then had Nightmist wipe them out in one go with an out-of-turn card play. Good stuff), so it all works out. Even when he eventually went down, his third incap power did some major damage. Nightmist hammered damn near everything with Oblivion -- Elder Ring + Imbued Fire + +1 to all fire damage, with a 2 pitched at everyone and 3 pitched at villains, she ended up doing 16 to Voss alone (Yaaay Amulet of the Elder Gods), leaving nothing in the way to keep Ra and Fanatic from burning the warlord down.</p>",
